{"name":"Dollar Bill","hex":"#85bb65","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dollar bill","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A note of currency worth one dollar."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dollar_bill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Australian one-dollar note","blocks":[{"text":"The Australian one-dollar note was introduced in 1966 due to decimalisation, to replace the 10-shilling note. The note was issued from its introduction in 1966 until its replacement by the one-dollar coin in 1984. Approximately 1.7 billion one-dollar notes were printed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Australian_%241_-_original_series_-_obverse.jpg/330px-Australian_%241_-_original_series_-_obverse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_one-dollar_note"},{"title":"Withdrawn Canadian banknotes","blocks":[{"text":"Banknotes that are no longer in issue in Canada, and are being removed from circulation, are said to be \"withdrawn from circulation\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Withdrawn_Canadian_banknotes"},{"title":"Dollar Bill (Jack White song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Dollar Bill\" is a song by the American musician Jack White, released as the second single from his seventh studio album Frozen Charlotte (2026) on June 10, 2026. It was announced via a 30-second preview upload to a channel named \"The Frozen Charlatan\", with the video simply titled \"$$$\"."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dollar_Bill_(Jack_White_song)"},{"title":"Dollar","blocks":[{"text":"Dollar is the name of more than 25 currencies and their base units. The United States dollar, named after the international currency known as the Spanish dollar, was established in 1792 and is the first so named that still survives. Others include the Australian dollar, Brunei dollar, Canadian dollar, Eastern Caribbean dollar, Hong Kong dollar, Jamaican dollar, Liberian dollar, Namibian dollar, New Taiwan dollar, New Zealand dollar, Singapore dollar, Trinidad and Tobago dollar, and several others. The symbol for most of those currencies is the dollar sign $; the same symbol is used by many countries using peso currencies."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ad/Joachimsthaler_1525.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dollar"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Australian_%241_-_original_series_-_reverse.jpg/500px-Australian_%241_-_original_series_-_reverse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Australian_%241_-_original_series_-_reverse.jpg/500px-Australian_%241_-_original_series_-_reverse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAustralian_%241_-_original_series_-_reverse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/NFLD_dollar_bill.jpg/500px-NFLD_dollar_bill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/NFLD_dollar_bill.jpg/500px-NFLD_dollar_bill.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"$1 Dominion of Newfoundland note issued in 1920","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANFLD_dollar_bill.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/25cents_canada1923.jpg/500px-25cents_canada1923.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/25cents_canada1923.jpg/1280px-25cents_canada1923.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/